  "conclusion": "On the full 1130-feature winner, the top-50 by gain (46 MAF + 4 sig) shows median eta2 0.0069 vs 0.0052 background (measurable 47 vs 902; MW p=0.106, not significant). The set is dominated by clean driver-gene features, but 3 VEP annotation-rate features with high center eta2 (0.12-0.57) are included at modest weight (1.3% of gain). The 3 SBS96 channels in the top-50 could not be measured (TCGA signature matrix absent); sensitivity shows the MW p-value stays >0.05 only if their eta2 < ~0.02, and the median comparison is invariant regardless. Combined with cross-center OVR (0.77-0.94), PCAWG consortium transfer, and unchanged center-stratified CV gap, the ranking is not batch-driven, but the manuscript's 'p=0.85, no excess' phrasing (from the 910-model top-50) should be softened to the winner's numbers with the 3-feature caveat disclosed."
